{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Cursed be he who dishonors his father, etc.</b> One needs to know why, out of all transgressions, He chose to pronounce curses specifically upon these. Also regarding forbidden relations, why did He single out only these for curses, when there are relations more severe than these, namely relations with a married woman (בא על אשת אישׁ)?" "Perhaps it is because He stated here only those transgressions that are hidden and concealed, and therefore He marked the first one and said <b>and places in secret</b>, for one who acts in a manner that would be exposed — behold, Israel have already entered into mutual surety for one another regarding that. And likewise what He said, <b>cursed be he who dishonors</b>, means that he does an act of disgrace to him in a manner that cannot be prosecuted against him in an earthly court. And likewise encroaching on a boundary is something that is not discernible. And likewise misleading a blind person on the road — no one sees. And likewise perverting the judgment of the lowly. And likewise lying with one's father's wife, and with an animal, and with one's sister, and one's mother-in-law — for all of them there is no awareness by others of his being with them to investigate it. And likewise one who strikes his fellow — Scripture specified to say <b>in secret</b>. And likewise one who takes a bribe, etc. — for example, if the court was evenly divided and one came and tilted the judgment with his reasoning because of a bribe — this too is among matters handed over to the heart, with no awareness by others." "And the reason He wrote <b>cursed be he who lies with an animal</b> between one's father's wife and one's sister is to say that the matter of one's father's wife and one's sister is as far removed as lying with an animal, which is a thing foreign and abhorrent to human nature:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:19:31.312575151Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}